# Normalize line endings to LF for all text files
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly mark binary files
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary

# Fork rename overrides — always keep our version on upstream merges.
# These files are 100% pcvelz->braseidon / plugin-name renames; auto-merge
# would just regenerate the same conflicts every sync.
# Requires: `git config merge.ours.driver true` (set per-clone).
# Watch-out: `merge=ours` silently drops upstream changes (version bumps,
# new fields). scripts/sync-upstream.sh prints a drift diff after each merge.
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json merge=ours
.claude-plugin/plugin.json merge=ours
.github/FUNDING.yml merge=ours
.version-bump.json merge=ours

# NOT pinned on purpose: hooks/session-start. Its only fork delta is the
# namespace in one string, but the pin silently held back a Windows iconv fix
# for weeks. Let it conflict every sync — a one-line conflict is cheap, a
# swallowed upstream fix is not.

# Non-Claude AI tooling (Cursor, Codex, Gemini, Copilot, OpenCode) is DELETED
# from this fork — Claude Code only. gitattributes can't enforce deletions
# (delete-vs-modify = conflict; new upstream files under a purged dir merge in
# cleanly), so upstream merges go through scripts/sync-upstream.sh, which
# re-deletes everything on its PURGE list and auto-resolves those conflicts.
